<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:55:28Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Zelensky says Ukraine is ready for an energy ceasefire with Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1463b6da7a9b77d9c8b4ba71459593c1b46662d57e3ad85cca0a21bbc3d06055</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:55:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T21:38:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260922-zelensky-says-ukraine-is-ready-for-an-energy-ceasefire-with-russia--85f40fba8089.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260922-zelensky-says-ukraine-is-ready-for-an-energy-ceasefire-with-russia" /><summary type="html">On the sidelines of the UN General Assembly in New York on Tuesday, Ukraine's President Volodymyr Zelensky told journalists that Kyiv is ready to halt strikes on Russian energy infrastructure if Moscow does the same, with hopes to end the war before winter.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Guterres pleads for 'world built on interdependence' in final General Assembly address</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8317c232efdedf47074ee78b454f6798bd817772794622aee413f8542184cb48</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:55:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T21:02:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260922-un-secretary-general-guterres-calls-for-interdependence-in-final-general-assembly-address--e6568de3bc46.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260922-un-secretary-general-guterres-calls-for-interdependence-in-final-general-assembly-address" /><summary type="html">UN Secretary-General Antonio Guterres pleaded for “a world built on interdependence” Tuesday as he made his final address to the annual gathering of world leaders convening to face a formidable menu of challenges, from climate change and war to inequality and the rise of artificial intelligence.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>French government scales up targeted fuel price relief</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:93b04d5a3de2fc27e3fe8de64d56d6e16d3f7a24774ea07fecd44e262fe98bf2</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:55:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T20:54:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20260922-french-government-scales-up-targeted-fuel-price-relief--7501443e912f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20260922-french-government-scales-up-targeted-fuel-price-relief" /><summary type="html">Under pressure to help businesses and workers cope with soaring fuel prices, the French government has announced it will expand targeted energy relief for those most affected.  The new measures will cost €450 million, bringing the total so far to €1.4 billion. Meanwhile, as French president Emmanuel Macron calls for allowing more biofuels to be added to diesel, we speak with an expert on the potential environmental impact of a rapid ramp-up in biofuel use.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Viral NATO video falsely framed as ‘war propaganda’ against Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0a76ef88bfa6ec42732fd1b7f6750c0abf0416c8f708caf312f6b0d328f90ce6</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:55:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T20:44:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/viral-nato-video-falsely-framed-as-war-propaganda-against-russia-1--764414d9cbe1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/viral-nato-video-falsely-framed-as-war-propaganda-against-russia-1" /><summary type="html">A viral NATO video is being falsely framed online as “war propaganda”, with users accusing the Alliance of sharing a “promotional video” designed to prepare the public for imminent war with Russia. But the footage is not new: NATO published it in July 2024 for its 75th anniversary, and it’s been stripped of its original context. The claim comes as European leaders warn of growing Russian hybrid threats, including alleged drone, cyber and sabotage activity. Vedika Bahl explains in Truth or Fake.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>US refusing to give Sudan's de facto leader visa for UN</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c584a0d402dbf104cf6a259f2979a1fe246bfe4bb2e678d18b9c201773c2045e</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:55:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T20:13:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-refusing-to-give-sudan-s-de-facto-leader-visa-for-un--35682f8a2d46.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-refusing-to-give-sudan-s-de-facto-leader-visa-for-un" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition, the United States is withholding a visa for Sudanese army chief al-Burhan ahead of his scheduled UN appearance. Also, Ghana’s beefing up its drugs authority in the wake of  major drug busts in France, Belgium and South Africa. And it’s back-to-school season in Ivory Coast.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Macron urges world to 'stand firm' against 'abuse of power by empires' in final UN speech</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7999e3420d01cfd5ea6bd0e20d611aa0a4d9fdb9d8c58c01a4b59a59df02d536</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:55:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T20:08:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20260922-macron-urges-world-stand-firm-against-abuse-of-power-by-empires-final-un-speech--a71283dad1fd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260922-macron-urges-world-stand-firm-against-abuse-of-power-by-empires-final-un-speech" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron used his last address before the UN General Assembly as France's leader to urge the world's nations to stand alongside the United Nations in the face of a resurgent "law of the jungle". Macron also called for a moratorium on strikes on civilian and energy infrastructure in the Russia-Ukraine war and an "open-source" model for frontier AI independent of China and the US.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Trump's world? Leaders navigate consequences of US policy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b69afca54b328a03accfcc7a964a1da5b2921a24c3e458c4243ccd2f66e3caf9</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:54:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T18:14:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260922-trump-s-world-leaders-navigate-consequences-of-us-policy--bf2ad7c85eca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260922-trump-s-world-leaders-navigate-consequences-of-us-policy" /><summary type="html">A year ago, Donald Trump went to the rostrum of the United Nations General Assembly - and after taxing an axe to US aid and development funding, read the world the riot act. One Iran war later, the US president sticking to script with a speech that borrowed much of the language of last year. With citizens on five continents now feeling the pain at the pump, we'll ask what it will take to tame a global energy crisis whose potential spiral mirrors the contagion of hostilities from the Strait of Hormuz to the mouth of the Red Sea?</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>🔴Watch live: French President Emmanuel Macron addresses UN General Assembly</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a39ab564e9e7bd99d23f60c60528b96794a195c3e84d3699bcf0cf1d749daf9e</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:54:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T17:41:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260922-live-guterres-to-open-un-general-assembly-in-final-speech-of-his-mandate--57a3ef49f3db.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260922-live-guterres-to-open-un-general-assembly-in-final-speech-of-his-mandate" /></entry><entry><title>Iran, AI and the ICC: Trump makes threats, touts policies at UN General Assembly</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab4b3b64191511fa7bafae52455649f50f4c626d17e35e3ccff2050cf469e653</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:54:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T17:09:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260922-iran-ai-and-the-icc-trump-makes-threats-touts-policies-un-general-assembly--12d297e3d635.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260922-iran-ai-and-the-icc-trump-makes-threats-touts-policies-un-general-assembly" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump launched a full-throated defence of the deeply unpopular US-Israeli war against Iran before the UN General Assembly on Tuesday, claiming that Washington would reach a deal with Tehran after the upcoming US midterm elections. Trump also rejected the idea of global regulation of artificial intelligence, said the government of Cuba would soon "fall", and urged member countries of the International Criminal Court to "resign".</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>🔴Live: 'Nobody with a conscience can close their eyes to what is happening in Gaza', Erdogan tells UN</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7e1c5cb422dc09155d180db22ae82a82affb342b5b10702c57d06c9ed99608db</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:54:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T16:24:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260922-live-guterres-to-open-un-general-assembly-in-final-speech-of-his-mandate--57a3ef49f3db.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260922-live-guterres-to-open-un-general-assembly-in-final-speech-of-his-mandate" /></entry><entry><title>Iran: Trump believes in an agreement after US midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f6bc8aaa4cc3f94ffb9b70caf1c24a02a33ba9ce048fe86bc95ac7c391f02cfc</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:54:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T16:17:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-iran-trump-believes-in-an-agreement-after-us-midterms--aa11d208ea3e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-iran-trump-believes-in-an-agreement-after-us-midterms" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump told the United Nations General Assembly on Tuesday that he would have to decide whether to “annihilate” Iran if Tehran fails to reach a deal to end the war in the Middle East.
 
He added that he believed an agreement was possible after the US midterm elections in November.</summary></entry><entry><title>REPLAY: Trump defends Iran war, attacks ICC in UN speech</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8fa3a434ceac78be77fb37eea0dbe3ae7c13b36445bd23cf8c343f79c98a6b6d</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:54:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T16:13:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-replay-trump-defends-iran-war-attacks-icc-in-un-speech--62e72858513d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-replay-trump-defends-iran-war-attacks-icc-in-un-speech" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump called Tuesday for all nations that are part of the International Criminal Court to quit the body, calling it "out of control." He also used the speech to argue that the war with Iran prevented Tehran from obtaining a nuclear weapon and warn that he could "annihilate the Islamic Republic" if no deal is reached to end the conflict. Watch his speech in full above.</summary></entry><entry><title>How is the EU responding to record fuel prices?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:78eaef24a39b2a4f255c60c0ea34e1bd5af1bd1a72b19194d73fb0c853607e64</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:54:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T16:07:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260922-how-is-the-eu-approaching-record-fuel-prices--5f583fca1c35.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260922-how-is-the-eu-approaching-record-fuel-prices" /><summary type="html">Fuel prices have hit record highs across Europe in recent days, driven by soaring oil prices amid the war in the Middle East and Ukrainian strikes on Russian refineries. However, the scale of the increases, as well as the measures taken to address them, varies significantly from one EU country to another. Here’s why.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Syrian man reunited with secret library hidden for 15 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:12a9dbd64ba61c34e32dfe1f7dddc0e4df67d5aef4c917c49a281ecdeb160e74</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:54:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T15:15:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-syrian-man-reunited-with-secret-library-hidden-for-15-years--4bc11dedc9dc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-syrian-man-reunited-with-secret-library-hidden-for-15-years" /><summary type="html">A Syrian man has been reunited with his collection of over 100 Islamic texts, science books and poems,15 years after sealing the collection behind a wall. Mustafa Khaled Alwan had built to conceal the library, which would likely have landed in prison, or worse, under Bashar al-Assad's rule.</summary></entry><entry><title>Lady Diana: Spencer’s memoir on Diana reignites royal controversy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ac05a2599c24b10f7c090a2420ac5237c27724a4ddba6d82764c0f65961e4505</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:54:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T14:59:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-lady-diana-spencer-s-memoir-on-diana-reignites-royal-controversy--b74044b1ff2d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-lady-diana-spencer-s-memoir-on-diana-reignites-royal-controversy" /><summary type="html">Prince Charles married with Lady Diana in 1981. The couple divorced in 1996 and a decade later Charles married Camilla Parker Bowles, now Queen Camilla. 
 
Spencer has long clashed with the royals over their treatment of his older sister.</summary></entry><entry><title>UN climate change body accused of conflict of interest, Saudi influence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c80c6d97c862a3e95e915673377497ef0e90a5226ac49e1b98e847d9cc3119f9</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:54:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T14:38:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-un-climate-change-body-accused-of-conflict-of-interest-saudi-influence--63663ec056ab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-un-climate-change-body-accused-of-conflict-of-interest-saudi-influence" /><summary type="html">An investigation conducted by the Guardian is raising questions about potential conflicts of interest among experts helping produce the next major assessment from the UN’s Inter-governmental Panel on Climate Change. Out of the 223 lead authors in the part of the body which assesses how emissions can be reduced or removed, 20 have a strong conflict of interest, according to the investigation, with more than half linked to Saudi institutions, including two employees of oil giant Saudi Aramco.</summary></entry><entry><title>Guterres delivers 'message to superpowers' in last UN General Assembly speech</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1552c437a38128d597c6b96ef6c5b08a7412452c1169d14de293a1f0218d3b5c</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:54:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T14:28:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-guterres-delivers-message-to-superpowers-in-last-un-general-assembly-speech--e5335de47362.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-guterres-delivers-message-to-superpowers-in-last-un-general-assembly-speech" /><summary type="html">UN Secretary-General Antonio Guterres pleaded for “a world built on interdependence” as he made his final address Tuesday to the General Assembly, a yearly gathering of world leaders, in a message that was largely intended for the world's superpowers, says France 24's UN correspondent Jessica Le Masurier.</summary></entry><entry><title>🔴Live: Trump set to defend Iran war in speech before UN General Assembly</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:68577248b12a12e83a34b7b30a451c9bd31003600939f22f53c7d0bfa0468146</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:54:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T14:26:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260922-live-guterres-to-open-un-general-assembly-in-final-speech-of-his-mandate--57a3ef49f3db.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260922-live-guterres-to-open-un-general-assembly-in-final-speech-of-his-mandate" /></entry><entry><title>REPLAY: UN chief Guterres makes final address to the General Assembly</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d62700f831a015ba0f269c974ec1973dce5806ff47f179a657657140608590f0</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:54:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T14:11:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-replay-un-chief-guterres-makes-final-address-to-the-general-assembly--53ca6bc1fe8c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-replay-un-chief-guterres-makes-final-address-to-the-general-assembly" /><summary type="html">United Nations Secretary-General Antonio Guterres used ​his final address to the General Assembly on Tuesday to urge world leaders to regulate artificial intelligence, end wars, focus on climate change and overhaul UN institutions he warned are struggling to confront mounting global challenges. Watch his speech in full above.</summary></entry><entry><title>From slavery to today: The Black women who shaped America</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed35649d175969c65049c36ab6863dc72f999b3860b837058edd16fc300b28c6</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:54:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T14:06:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260922-from-slavery-to-today-the-black-women-who-shaped-america--559ae654c697.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260922-from-slavery-to-today-the-black-women-who-shaped-america" /><summary type="html">"If you don’t understand the history of Black women, you don’t understand the history of America." Those words from Nobel Prize-winning novelist Toni Morrison open Sasha Bonét's debut memoir, "The Waterbearers". The New York writer traces three generations of Black women in her family: her grandmother Betty Jean, the daughter of formerly enslaved people in Louisiana who went on to raise eleven children; her mother Connie, who sought a middle-class life in majority-white Houston; and Sasha herself, now raising her daughter Sofia in New York.</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>Guatemala receives first US arms in nearly 50 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8159247a37cf42d251c9577107b8d744f6a315654bb3b0f23ded4f16c6ff5650</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:54:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T14:05:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-guatemala-receives-first-us-arms-in-nearly-50-years--6670e6930b1b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-guatemala-receives-first-us-arms-in-nearly-50-years" /><summary type="html">Guatemala on Monday received the first batch of military weapons from the US in almost five decades. It ends an arms embargo implemented by the US due to human rights violations made during Guatemala's civil war. The US has continued to cooperate with Guatemala in recent years in the battle against drug trafficking.</summary></entry><entry><title>'UN unable to bring peace to conflicts: We haven’t seen this level of violence in decades’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c3861f5ae53c9f392e396e5b98c7c155b56fb0d4f3d8ef0bf1e7058dbdfd303b</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:54:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T14:04:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/un-unable-to-bring-peace-to-conflicts-we-haven-t-seen-this-level-of-violence-in-decades--6d0a22913e8c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/un-unable-to-bring-peace-to-conflicts-we-haven-t-seen-this-level-of-violence-in-decades" /><summary type="html">Rochelle Ferguson Bouyahi is pleased to welcome Fanny Badache, Researcher at Sciences Po and Lecturer at the University of Geneva. The UN mandate is international peace and security, yet its ability to fulfill that mandate ultimately depends on the cooperation of sovereign states, namely the five powerful permanent members of the Security Council. As the UN is confronted with an increasingly fragmented, volatile and unpredictable international order, Badache argues that when those powers are divided, the mechanisms designed to enable collective security can instead produce paralysis.</summary></entry><entry><title>US threatens South Sudan with sanctions over aid obstruction</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c3a7fe463b7679a5dc7ee0011ad48e3b40df6be57333f9dfdf5b3f2c505c163c</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:54:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T13:34:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-us-threatens-south-sudan-with-sanctions-over-aid-obstruction--7dafdfc0aa9c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-us-threatens-south-sudan-with-sanctions-over-aid-obstruction" /><summary type="html">The United States has threatened to impose sanctions on South Sudan over alleged obstruction of humanitarian assistance, accusing officials at national, state and local levels of treating aid as a source of revenue.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ladin: Dolomites villages refuse to give up on ancient language</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2b8558801d982ae9313cdb5b0b328e1337a46b9b223d7e6ed24e87d4f1aa0436</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:54:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T13:30:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260922-ladin-dolomites-villages-refuse-to-give-up-on-ancient-language--e899b61b23c1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260922-ladin-dolomites-villages-refuse-to-give-up-on-ancient-language" /><summary type="html">Year after year, the mountains of the Dolomites become more popular with tourists. Amid millions of visitors, 30,000 inhabitants speak a language only they understand: Ladin, one of the oldest minority languages in Europe.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry></feed>
